# LOCK SCOPE — pcampus-ui Library Authoring Rules

> This is the **source** library. These rules govern what goes IN, not what comes out.
> Consumer rules: `Pcampus-Agent-OS/.cursor/rules/pcampus-ui-lock.mdc`

## Namespace rule

Every CSS custom property defined in this library MUST use the `--pcampus-` prefix.

```css
/* ✓ correct */
--pcampus-color-primary: #3B7DD8;
--pcampus-radius-md: 8px;

/* ✗ forbidden */
--color-primary: #3B7DD8;   /* no prefix — collides with consumer */
--radius-md: 8px;
```

## Component authoring rules

Every component MUST:
- Accept and spread `className` prop (no style lock-in for consumers)
- Use Tailwind utility classes via `className` — never `style={}` for visual properties
- Use `var(--pcampus-color-*)` for any color not expressible as Tailwind utility
- Use `clsx()` for conditional class composition

```tsx
// ✓ correct
export function Button({ className, variant = 'primary', ...props }) {
  return (
    <button
      className={clsx(variantClass[variant], 'rounded-pcampus-md px-4 py-2 transition-colors', className)}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}

// ✗ forbidden
export function Button({ variant, ...props }) {
  return <button style={{ backgroundColor: '#3B7DD8' }} {...props} />;
}
```

## Chart rules

All chart components MUST:
- Use `chartColors` from `src/charts/colors.ts` — which references `var(--pcampus-color-*)`
- Wrap with `<ResponsiveContainer>` from recharts
- Accept `color` / `colors` prop override for domain customization
- Never hardcode `#hex` in chart source

## Motion rules

All animation MUST:
- Define keyframes in `src/motion/keyframes.css` with `pcampus-` prefix: `@keyframes pcampus-shimmer`
- Use `var(--pcampus-duration-*)` and `var(--pcampus-ease-*)` — no hardcoded `ms` or `cubic-bezier` in components
- Export `useMotionPreference()` hook for accessibility
- Map to Tailwind `animate-*` utilities via `@theme inline` in `theme.css`

## Tier map — build in this order

```
1. Tokens       src/tokens/index.css            --pcampus-* vars
2. Theme        src/styles/theme.css            @theme inline mapping
3. Primitives   src/primitives/                 Button, Card, Input, ...
4. Forms        src/forms/                      Select, Checkbox, ...
5. Overlays     src/overlays/                   Modal, Toast, Tooltip, ...
6. Layout       src/layout/                     AppShell, Sidebar, ...
7. Charts       src/charts/                     FunnelChart, KpiChart, ...
8. Motion       src/motion/                     keyframes, hooks, presets
```

Higher tiers consume lower tiers. Never import upward.

## Two entry points — maintain both

| File | Contains | For |
|------|----------|-----|
| `dist/index.css` | Pre-built utilities (full Tailwind output) | Services without Tailwind |
| `dist/theme.css` | `@theme inline` only, no `@import "tailwindcss"` | Services with their own Tailwind v4 |

Do NOT merge these. A service uses one or the other — never both.

## Scope gate — two-service rule

A component graduates to pcampus-ui when 2+ Pcampus services need it.
Exception: foundational tokens, theme, and motion always belong here regardless of consumer count.

## FORBIDDEN in this library

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| Consumer product names in code / vars / comments | Platform stays generic ([platform-consumer.mdc](platform-consumer.mdc)) |
| `@import "tailwindcss"` inside `theme.css` | Consumer provides Tailwind — we must not double-import |
| Hardcoded `#hex` anywhere except token definitions | Tokens are the only place colors live |
| `style={}` in component JSX for visual properties | Blocks pseudo-state styling |
| Framework-specific imports (Next.js `Link`, React Router) | Library must be framework-agnostic |
| CSS variable names without `--pcampus-` prefix | Collision with consumer namespace |
